After doing a lab or making changes myself:

git status                      # see what changed
git add week4/day3.ipynb        # stage specific files (avoid `git add .`)
git commit -m "week4 day3: litellm + openrouter"
git push                        # sends it to your fork on GitHub


Before starting new material: Pull from Eds updates

git status                      # should say "nothing to commit"
git fetch upstream              # download Ed's changes, doesn't touch your files
git merge upstream/main         # combine them with yours
git push                        # update your fork

uv sync

